//! The supervisor: how Qnet 2.0 runs a solver, watches it, stops it and reports on it.
//!
//! In 0.90.34 every run was a bash wrapper generated by `QnetGUIApp.runScript` or `silentScript`
//! and typed into the user's interactive shell; `TerminalModel` then coordinated with it through
//! done, pid, status and output files polled every 500 ms (`beginRun`, `tickRun`,
//! `drainActiveStatusInbox`, `captureActiveRunGroup`, `cancelSurvivorsOutstanding`,
//! `cancelActiveRun`, `signalActiveRun`, `finishRun`). Decision D1 has the app start solvers itself,
//! so this module replaces the wrapper and that coordination while keeping every outcome the user
//! saw: single flight across tabs with 0.90.34's refusal sentence, every lifecycle message routed to
//! the launching tab, the SIGINT, SIGTERM at 1.5 s, SIGKILL at 3 s ladder on the run's own process
//! group, a run that is over only when its group is gone, the stderr policy of
//! `runWithStderrOnFailure`, progress from `-P` files every 500 ms, the outcome sentences of
//! `TerminalRunSummary`, and the run-label maps. What 2.0 changes, and why, is said in each
//! submodule's header; the ledger rows are RUN-018…RUN-055 (supervision), FILE-020…026, SH-079…087,
//! LOG-005…008 and INV-009…011, 023, 049…058.
//!
//! The pieces, bottom up:
//! - [`cancel`]: the Stop token, live before the first process exists.
//! - [`process`]: one program in its own process group, output streamed, the ladder.
//! - [`job`]: a run's steps, output sink and archive, temporary files, progress poller.
//! - [`registry`]: single flight, the owning tab, and the events it receives.
//! - [`stderr`], [`summary`], [`progress`], [`labels`]: the pure rules and words.
//!
//! The display-precision filter, banners, tables and per-method commands belong to
//! `qnet_core::output` and the method modules; they feed a [`job::Job`] through its output and an
//! [`job::OutputSink`].
//!
//! A typical launch:
//!
//! ```no_run
//! use std::sync::Arc;
//! use qnet_runner::supervisor::*;
//!
//! let registry = RunRegistry::new();
//! let reporter: Reporter = Arc::new(|event: &RunEvent| println!("{event:?}"));
//! let owner = RunOwner { id: "tab-1".into(), title: "Tandem".into() };
//! if let Ok(ticket) = registry.begin("qna", owner, reporter) {
//!     let report = run_job(ticket, Box::new(NullSink), |job| {
//!         job.status("Running QNA...", Severity::Info);
//!         let step = Step::new(ProcessSpec::new("/path/to/bna_qna").arg("input.qna").arg("-c"))
//!             .stderr_policy("QNA");
//!         match job.run_step(&step) {
//!             Ok(outcome) => outcome.shell_code(),
//!             Err(e) => {
//!                 job.could_not_start(format!("QNA could not start: {e}"));
//!                 -1
//!             }
//!         }
//!     });
//!     println!("{}", report.summary.text());
//! }
//! ```

